WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.315
Runtime monitoring looks for behavior inconsistent with the workload and its security profile.

00:00:07.315 --> 00:00:21.692
Useful signals include unexpected processes, privilege or capability use, unusual child-process chains, changes to protected paths, access to host resources, or network connections outside the application baseline.

00:00:21.692 --> 00:00:27.997
Kubernetes audit logs show API requests, identities, resources, and authorization outcomes.

00:00:27.997 --> 00:00:35.816
Admission decisions, deployment changes, service-account activity, secret access, and node-management operations add orchestration context.

00:00:35.816 --> 00:00:42.122
Node telemetry contributes kernel, process, filesystem, authentication, runtime, and integrity evidence.

00:00:42.122 --> 00:00:51.454
Alerts should include workload, image, namespace, service account, node, cluster, action, policy, time, and related deployment change.

00:00:51.454 --> 00:01:03.813
Triage asks whether the behavior is expected, whether the isolation boundary was crossed, what privileges were available, and which assets may be affected.

00:01:03.813 --> 00:01:07.597
Containment and recovery need preplanned choices.

00:01:07.597 --> 00:01:18.947
Teams may stop or isolate a workload, restrict network access, drain a node, rotate credentials, or replace infrastructure from known-good definitions.

00:01:18.947 --> 00:01:25.757
The correct action depends on evidence, application availability, tenancy, and orchestration impact.

00:01:25.757 --> 00:01:29.541
Preserve evidence before volatile data disappears.

00:01:29.541 --> 00:01:38.369
Retain relevant audit and runtime events, image identity, deployment specifications, node context, timelines, and analyst decisions.

00:01:38.369 --> 00:01:45.683
Coordinate collection so it does not overwrite evidence or cause unnecessary production disruption.

00:01:45.683 --> 00:01:50.980
Practice response with platform, application, security, and reliability teams.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:02:00.312
Afterward, correct configuration, rebuild images or nodes, rotate exposed trust, improve detections, and update the threat model.

00:02:00.312 --> 00:02:08.636
Monitoring is effective when it supports decisive containment and trustworthy recovery, not simply more alerts.
